2f:["$","p",null,{"children":"You can find the URL path details in the HubSpot Developer’s documentation. The URL path shown in the examples below is specific to one HubSpot object, i.e., a contact. However, if you want to work with a different object (such as companies, deals, etc.), simply refer to the API documentation link provided."}]
30:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Note:"}]," How to construct URL path based on Base URL of the application has been explained above in the GET method section. Please refer to that."]}]
31:["$","p",null,{"children":["The ID in the URL path corresponds to the specific record you want to target. For example, in the case of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"v3/objects/contacts/328766938858"}],", the number ",["$","code",null,{"children":"328766938858"}]," represents the unique ID of a contact. You will need to replace this ID with the ID of the contact (or any other object) you wish to retrieve, update, or interact with."]}]
